$20=20\cdot20+0\cdot(-20),$
$0=20\cdot(-6)+(-20)\cdot(-7),$
$20=20\cdot(-7)+(-20)\cdot8$ and so on.
Subtracting the last and fourth equations gets
$20+20=20(-6-8)=20\cdot(-14)=20\cdot(-1+12).$
Thus, there are $13$ lattice points in the right-most triangle.
In general, if we consider a triangle with height $h=\sqrt{3}x+2k$ for some constant $k$ and width $\sqrt{3}x,$ then the number of lattice points inside it is $x-1.$ Thus, the number of lattice points in the whole diagram is
$2\sum_{k=-10}^{10}(x-1)=22\sum_{k=0}^{10}(x-1)=55\cdot2\left(\frac{0+(10-1)h}{2}\right)=55\frac{(10-0)(10+1+10)}{2}=55(21)(5)=5775$  triangles.
